EXPLANATION = {"title": "Bond Angle", "principle": "Backbone bond angles (N-CA-C, CA-C-N, O-C-N) stay within 18 degrees RMSD of Engh-Huber ideals.", "rationale": "The pinned code (definition v2, WP-SCI-1) measures the RMS angular deviation of backbone bond angles across core residues: intra-residue N(i)-CA(i)-C(i), peptide O(i)-C(i)-N(i+1) using the NEXT residue's nitrogen, and CA(i)-C(i)-N(i+1) over valid sequential pairs only. Definition v1 used the same residue's nitrogen for O-C-N, which is a non-bonded pseudo-angle. LAW-120 is currently CONTAINED (a measured veto cannot independently issue an authoritative VETO) until the corrected metric is re-validated by the v24 calibration and the independent validation protocol."}
